WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.048
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Writing Skills.

2
00:00:05.348 --> 00:00:08.781
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.081 --> 00:00:15.135
Unit fourteen: Advantages and Disadvantages. Today you will write about both sides of a topic.

4
00:00:15.435 --> 00:00:17.925
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.867 --> 00:00:22.192
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.050 --> 00:00:24.086
Advantage.

7
00:00:25.083 --> 00:00:27.594
Advantage means a good point or benefit.

8
00:00:28.183 --> 00:00:30.276
One advantage is lower cost.

9
00:00:30.883 --> 00:00:33.454
Your turn. Say: Advantage.

10
00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:37.220
Advantage.

11
00:00:37.983 --> 00:00:39.147
Disadvantage.

12
00:00:40.150 --> 00:00:42.823
Disadvantage means a bad point or drawback.

13
00:00:43.417 --> 00:00:45.312
One disadvantage is noise.

14
00:00:45.917 --> 00:00:48.848
Your turn. Say: Disadvantage.

15
00:00:51.700 --> 00:00:52.933
Disadvantage.

16
00:00:53.683 --> 00:00:54.650
Benefit.

17
00:00:55.650 --> 00:00:57.835
Benefit means something that helps you.

18
00:00:58.450 --> 00:01:00.020
There are many benefits.

19
00:01:00.617 --> 00:01:02.944
Your turn. Say: Benefit.

20
00:01:05.800 --> 00:01:06.639
Benefit.

21
00:01:07.383 --> 00:01:08.222
Drawback.

22
00:01:09.217 --> 00:01:11.785
Drawback means a problem or negative point.

23
00:01:12.383 --> 00:01:14.313
A drawback is the price.

24
00:01:14.917 --> 00:01:17.395
Your turn. Say: Drawback.

25
00:01:20.233 --> 00:01:21.385
Drawback.

26
00:01:22.150 --> 00:01:22.977
Whereas.

27
00:01:23.983 --> 00:01:26.714
Whereas means used to compare two different things.

28
00:01:27.317 --> 00:01:30.582
City life is busy, whereas village life is calm.

29
00:01:31.183 --> 00:01:33.940
Your turn. Say: Whereas.

30
00:01:36.800 --> 00:01:37.708
Whereas.

31
00:01:38.450 --> 00:01:39.765
On the other hand.

32
00:01:40.750 --> 00:01:43.632
On the other hand means used to give the opposite view.

33
00:01:44.217 --> 00:01:46.367
On the other hand, it is expensive.

34
00:01:46.983 --> 00:01:49.763
Your turn. Say: On the other hand.

35
00:01:52.600 --> 00:01:53.775
On the other hand.

36
00:01:54.517 --> 00:01:55.436
Balanced.

37
00:01:56.450 --> 00:01:58.647
Balanced means fair to both sides.

38
00:01:59.250 --> 00:02:00.808
Write a balanced essay.

39
00:02:01.417 --> 00:02:04.173
Your turn. Say: Balanced.

40
00:02:07.033 --> 00:02:08.104
Balanced.

41
00:02:08.850 --> 00:02:09.526
Weigh.

42
00:02:10.517 --> 00:02:13.143
Weigh means to think about good and bad points.

43
00:02:13.750 --> 00:02:15.773
Weigh both sides before deciding.

44
00:02:16.383 --> 00:02:18.594
Your turn. Say: Weigh.

45
00:02:21.433 --> 00:02:22.307
Weigh.

46
00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:26.658
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:27.517 --> 00:02:31.072
Visal, how do I write about advantages and disadvantages?

48
00:02:32.183 --> 00:02:41.143
Plan two sides. Write one paragraph for the advantages and one for the disadvantages. Keep it balanced.

49
00:02:42.250 --> 00:02:43.576
Which phrases help?

50
00:02:44.683 --> 00:02:54.557
Use one advantage is, another benefit is, on the other hand and one drawback is. They show the contrast clearly.

51
00:02:55.650 --> 00:02:57.046
Do I give my opinion?

52
00:02:58.150 --> 00:03:04.158
Often yes, in the conclusion. Weigh both sides, then say which is stronger and why.

53
00:03:05.300 --> 00:03:07.102
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:07.950 --> 00:03:10.495
Grammar focus: Showing contrast.

55
00:03:10.795 --> 00:03:12.029
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:12.717 --> 00:03:15.854
City life is exciting, whereas village life is peaceful.

57
00:03:16.750 --> 00:03:20.842
Online study is flexible. On the other hand, it can feel lonely.

58
00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:27.773
Use whereas, while and on the other hand to compare two sides. Give each side its own paragraph.

59
00:03:28.517 --> 00:03:32.086
Be careful! Don't say: City is noisy whereas.

60
00:03:34.033 --> 00:03:37.740
Say: The city is noisy, whereas the village is quiet.

61
00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:39.691
Complete both sides.

62
00:03:40.500 --> 00:03:43.210
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:45.198
Online Study.

64
00:03:45.498 --> 00:03:47.521
Vuthy writes about online study.

65
00:03:48.533 --> 00:03:51.299
One advantage is that it is flexible and cheap.

66
00:03:52.300 --> 00:03:55.298
Another benefit is that students save travel time.

67
00:03:56.300 --> 00:03:58.416
On the other hand, it can feel lonely.

68
00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:02.119
Overall, he thinks the benefits are stronger.

69
00:04:03.233 --> 00:04:07.119
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:07.983 --> 00:04:09.890
An advantage is a good blank.

71
00:04:10.190 --> 00:04:13.402
A, cost. B, street. C, point.

72
00:04:16.967 --> 00:04:18.664
The answer is C: point.

73
00:04:19.817 --> 00:04:21.677
A drawback is a blank point.

74
00:04:21.977 --> 00:04:25.166
A, negative. B, happy. C, long.

75
00:04:28.700 --> 00:04:30.804
The answer is A: negative.

76
00:04:31.950 --> 00:04:34.089
Whereas compares two blank things.

77
00:04:34.389 --> 00:04:37.694
A, empty. B, different. C, same.

78
00:04:41.233 --> 00:04:42.792
The answer is B: different.

79
00:04:43.950 --> 00:04:46.542
A balanced essay is fair to both blank.

80
00:04:46.842 --> 00:04:50.414
A, doors. B, years. C, sides.

81
00:04:53.967 --> 00:04:56.036
The answer is C: sides.

82
00:04:57.183 --> 00:04:59.090
Vuthy writes about blank study.

83
00:04:59.390 --> 00:05:03.554
A, online. B, night. C, farm.

84
00:05:07.100 --> 00:05:08.983
The answer is A: online.

85
00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:13.514
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:14.350 --> 00:05:16.233
How do you write about two sides?

87
00:05:25.050 --> 00:05:26.411
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:26.711 --> 00:05:38.468
I plan the advantages and disadvantages separately and write a paragraph for each. I use phrases like on the other hand and whereas. In the conclusion I weigh both sides and give my view.

89
00:05:38.768 --> 00:05:40.292
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:41.183 --> 00:05:44.857
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and showing contrast.

91
00:05:45.157 --> 00:05:50.364
Today's value is open-mindedness. Listen to new ideas before you judge them.

92
00:05:50.664 --> 00:05:53.119
See you in Unit fifteen. Goodbye!

93
00:05:53.419 --> 00:05:56.141
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

